<title>UK: Courtaulds, Pilkington may exit FTSE 100.</title>
<headline>Courtaulds, Pilkington may exit FTSE 100.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemicals group Courtaulds Plc and building materials firm Pilkington Plc are in line to be dropped from the key FTSE 100 index at the next membership meeting for the make-up of the index on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A member of the committee told Reuters on Tuesday that the sharp fallback in the value of the two companies since the last quarterly meeting was held meant they were likely to be replaced. The hottest contenders to take their places are the business services group Hays Plc and Mercury Asset Management Plc.</p>
</text>
